MozcForAndroid
==============

This application bundles software and data derived from the projects below.

Mozc
---
Mozc is licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
Copyright 2010-2025 Google Inc.
Source: https://github.com/google/mozc

The application bundles the Mozc JNI library (libmozc.so, built from target //android/jni:mozc.arm64)
and the Mozc data file (assets/mozc.data, built from target //data_manager/oss:mozc_dataset_for_oss),
built from the pinned submodule in mozc/.

Bundled dictionaries (baked into assets/mozc.data at build time)
--------------------------------------------------------------

- dic-nico-intersection-pixiv
  Source: https://github.com/ncaq/dic-nico-intersection-pixiv
  Dictionary of words appearing in both Niconico Pedia and Pixiv Encyclopedia.
  The upstream project does not claim copyright over the generated dictionary.

- google-ime-user-dictionary-ja-en
  Source: https://github.com/KEINOS/google-ime-user-dictionary-ja-en
  A Japanese-English word list derived from the Electronic Dictionary of Japanese (EDICT),
  licensed CC BY-SA 3.0.

- mozcdic-ut-jawiki
  Source: https://github.com/utuhiro78/mozcdic-ut-jawiki
  Readings and surfaces harvested from the Japanese Wikipedia.
  Licensed CC BY-SA 3.0.

The three dictionaries are not shipped as assets; Gradle's generateSystemDictionary task compiles
the fetched TSVs in third_party/dictionaries/ into the system dictionary at build time. See
scripts/fetch_dictionaries.py and NOTICE for the details of how they are fetched.
